    "H7 experimental bending shells: 3 mm board, nominal material stiffness, 5 mm corner slots (about 2 mm clearance after both collision radii). The earlier 3 mm slots left zero physical clearance and jammed adjacent upright flaps. Structural crease constraints attach the board to the box; there are no constraints between flaps. Interlocking is not certified by the scene alone.",
    "Native crease attachment is a 1 mm band with a 5 mm transition row and area-weighted vertex mass. The previous two uniform pinned rows fixed 19-25 mm of board, which overlapped the neighboring flap before it could bend into a separate layer. Geometry and mass remain explicit; this is an uncalibrated cardboard model, not a latch.",
    "Free edges stop 3 mm short of the box centre line to account for finite board thickness. Opposite flaps otherwise overlap at the common centre, obstructing a cyclic weave; adjacent overlap regions and the 20 x 15 x 12 cm box are retained.",
    "The 3 mm finite-thickness crease uses a nominal 4.8 mm neutral-axis offset above the rim, providing 3 mm more clearance than the earlier zero-clearance root. This removes parent-wall jamming without disabling wall/flap contact or changing the motor caps. It is an explicit geometry approximation, not a measured crease calibration."
  ],
